{"name":"Honeycomb Yellow","hex":"#de9c52","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"honeycomb","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A substance made by bees (clade Anthophila) primarily from beeswax which has hexagonal cells to hold their larvae, and for storing pollen and honey to feed the larvae and themselves when other food is scarce; it is also eaten by humans as part of comb-honey;  a single sheet made up of two layers of this substance.","Something resembling honeycomb (noun sense 1) in having numerous cells or small holes."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To riddle (something) with small holes, especially in a pattern resembling a honeycomb (noun sense 1); also, to cause (something) to become hollow or weakened in this way.\n\nTo bore cavities or tunnels inside (something).","To riddle (something) with small holes, especially in a pattern resembling a honeycomb (noun sense 1); also, to cause (something) to become hollow or weakened in this way."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honeycomb"},{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Honeycomb","blocks":[{"text":"A honeycomb is a mass of hexagonal prismatic cells built from beeswax by honey bees in their nests to contain their brood and stores of honey and pollen."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Honey_comb.jpg/330px-Honey_comb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honeycomb","wikidata":"Q123339"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow","wikidata":"Q943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Honeycombs_for_Sale_-_Saraeyn_-_Iranian_Azerbaijan_-_Iran_%287421128352%29.jpg/500px-Honeycombs_for_Sale_-_Saraeyn_-_Iranian_Azerbaijan_-_Iran_%287421128352%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Honeycombs_for_Sale_-_Saraeyn_-_Iranian_Azerbaijan_-_Iran_%287421128352%29.jpg/1280px-Honeycombs_for_Sale_-_Saraeyn_-_Iranian_Azerbaijan_-_Iran_%287421128352%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Honeycombs_for_Sale_-_Saraeyn_-_Iranian_Azerbaijan_-_Iran_%287421128352%29.jpg/500px-Honeycombs_for_Sale_-_Saraeyn_-_Iranian_Azerbaijan_-_Iran_%287421128352%29.jpg?utm_sourc